<title>HONG KONG: CDL Hotels 1996 net rises 39.9 percent.</title>
<headline>CDL Hotels 1996 net rises 39.9 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   32.98	 vs 25.99 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.0	   vs 5.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  152.66 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    615.69	vs 439.96 (see note)</p>
<p>    Turnover		     5,291.06    vs 3,811.18 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		 CDL Hotels International Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 5-11</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   July 9</p>
<p>NOTE - CDL Hotels International has hotel interests in Singapore, Taiwan, Malaysia and the Philippines.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain from the reduction in the company's interest in subsidiary Millennium &amp; Copthorne Hotels Plc when the unit's shares were offered to the public and listed on the London Stock Exchange in April 1996.</p>
<p>Comparative figures have been restated to adjust for the changes in basis of accounting for foreign exchange contracts entered into by the company for the purpose of hedging against its foreign investment in subsidiary companies.</p>
</text>
